    "source": "vendor",
    "notes": "ESMU (battery stack management unit) per vendor doc ESMU_MODBUS_V2.1_EN (TCP). ESMU is the Modbus TCP server (default port 502), unit id 1 = stack object; it drops the socket after 30 s without a request (poller reconnects automatically; keep pollIntervalSec < 30). Addresses are as printed (decimal), treated as PDU addresses — if the field unit answers illegal-address, subtract 1. Current/temperature registers are biased (offset −1600 A / −40 °C) — decoded via RegisterDef.offset. Current sign assumed + = discharging (verify on site). No stack power register exists in the protocol (P = V × I). BMS system state (reg 43): 0x00 init, 0x01 charging, 0x02 discharging, 0x03 ready, 0x04 string maintenance, 0x05 charge prohibited, 0x06 discharge prohibited, 0x07 charge+discharge prohibited, 0x08 fault, 0x09 fault recovery, 0x0A test mode, 0x0B powering off, 0x0C power-off complete. NOT mapped (monitoring-only integration): FC02 discrete alarm bits (system summary 1–80), FC06/10 control writes (breaker, power up/down, maintenance) and FC41 time sync — platform alarms derive from telemetry rules instead (e.g. bmsStatusCode = 8 → fault).",
